WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:02.300
If only Mark Ruffalo had a time machine.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:06.760
The actor who plays Bruce Banner and his alter
ego The Hulk is a notorious spoiler-spiller.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:08.420
So, obviously, spoilers ahead!

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:13.660
In June 2017, Ruffalo inadvertently gave away
the ending of Avengers: Infinity War during

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.099
a Good Morning America interview:

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:18.060
"Wait 'til you see this next one — everybody
dies."

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.840
"Dude, dude!"

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.200
"... Not everybody.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:21.700
No."

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.900
And in November 2017, he accidentally live-streamed
part of Thor: Ragnarok during the film's world

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:27.500
premiere.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.380
"You gave away the whole movie, didn't you?"

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.400
"Well, only the first ten minutes of it."

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:35.840
And then, during his October 2018 appearance
on The Late Show with Jimmy Fallon, Ruffalo

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.420
revealed the title of Avengers: Endgame before
it was officially announced:

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:46.680
"I think it's out there already: The title
of the next Avengers movie is: [Beep.]"

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.620
It's worth noting that Ruffalo actually said
"The Last Avenger," but that didn't stop Endgame

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.140
co-directors Joe and Anthony Russo from posting
a tweet that read:

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.140
"Mark, you're fired."

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:00.560
Well, at least he kept his mouth shut while
promoting Avengers: Endgame, right?

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:01.320
Wrong!

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:06.400
It turns out Ruffalo actually did spoil Avengers:
Endgame several weeks ago, when he blurted

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.540
out a major plot point from the end of the
film.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:13.240
In an interview with E! News alongside Captain
America actor Chris Evans and Nebula actress

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:17.470
Karen Gillan, Ruffalo revealed that the Russo
brothers had him shoot five different endings

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:18.220
for the film.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.760
He also revealed that the directing duo never
gave him a complete script.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.840
The actor said he didn't know the true conclusion
of Endgame during filming… and he claimed

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:30.159
that he'd have to wait until the movie opened
in theaters to find out which ending was ultimately

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:30.760
chosen.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:31.920
Ruffalo explained:

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.520
"I didn't even get a whole script of this
movie.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.280
I don't know why.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:40.060
The script I did get had dummy scenes in it."

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.600
The story checks out.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:45.800
The Russos have a history of withholding full
scripts from the actors, having done so with

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:49.250
Avengers: Infinity War to keep story secrets
close to the chest.

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:52.820
Anyway, at one point in the interview, Ruffalo
pointed to Evans and joked:

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.100
"He gets married in this!"

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:56.960
Ha… that's hilarious, right?

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:59.480
Captain America tying the knot in Avengers:
Endgame?

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:00.800
Like that would ever happen.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.060
Except it does happen.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:06.020
Though Ruffalo was offering an example of
one of the dummy scenes, he actually revealed

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.280
the real ending to the superhero ensemble.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:13.080
Avengers: Endgame reveals that Steve Rogers
retires from being Captain America after returning

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.460
each Infinity Stone to their proper places
in time.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:20.160
He chooses to remain in the past, reuniting
with his love Peggy Carter and growing old

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:20.660
with her.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:25.140
Steve later resurfaces five years after the
events of Infinity War, explaining to Sam

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.440
Wilson that he chose to go back in time to
live the life'd always wanted.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:31.020
When Steve shakes Sam's hand, we see a wedding
band.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:35.010
Steve stays mum on who the wife is, but a
dance sequence between he and Peggy at the

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.400
end of the film proves that she's the lady
in question.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:41.660
So, yeah — Mark Ruffalo totally spoiled
Endgame, but he probably didn't know he was

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.580
spoiling the film.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:46.880
It sounds like Ruffalo's script was chock
full of fake scenes and he had no way of knowing

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:47.760
which ones were real.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:51.300
Other actors in the MCU have been similarly
confused in the past.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:55.620
Let's go back in time to Tom Holland's April
2018 appearance on Jimmy Kimmel Live while

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.940
the cast was promoting Avengers: Infinity
War.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:02.060
Holland revealed that he didn't believe Spiderman
would ever wind up in an sci-fi tizzy with

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:02.620
Thanos:

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:07.060
"I was reading what I thought was a fake script
because it was like, 'Spider-Man's in space!'

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:10.020
So I didn't finish it, but I found out it
was real."

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:13.120
That's the catch-22 of the Russo brothers'
fake scripts.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:17.170
They succeed in keeping actors in the dark
and keeping spoilers from leaking, but they

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.600
totally confuse the cast to the point that
they don't know what's real or fake.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.480
Ruffalo clearly thought the idea of Captain
America getting married was too ridiculous

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:28.740
to be true, and he must've believed it was
a fake plot point that was okay to talk about.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:32.610
Taking all this into consideration, we can't
place too much blame on Ruffalo.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:35.980
Fingers crossed he doesn't get fake-fired
from the MCU a second time.

